om/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110252","id":3254457689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B-xVZ","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T16:12:27Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T16:12:27Z","body":"See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12665\n\nIt is not really a bug but a limitation of the polygon layout that the TileMap creates. The post processing can only work with what the polygon corridor is, and polygon corridor on a TileMap (or anything that adds many, many small, equal sized polygons) is commonly jagged and has problems with tie-breakers.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254457689/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254832906","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110252#issuecomment-3254832906","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110252","id":3254832906,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CAM8K","user":{"login":"RicardRC","id":35220750,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjIwNzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35220750?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC","html_url":"https://github.com/RicardRC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardRC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T17:45:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T17:45:55Z","body":"@smix8 yeah, I acknowledge this might be an existing limitation, so not a regression, nevertheless, this is pathfinding using A* and it starts with an optimal path, so postprocessing should not choose tie breakers in a manner that ends up creating a longer than optimal path (to me, this means there's a bug, because an engine feature does not produce the expected results). It should either be consistent or use some heuristic, but as is, it ends up a little silly.\n\n@AThousandShips this still happens in 6c9aa4c7d3b9b91cd50714c40eeb234874df7075","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254832906/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3282941470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110252#issuecomment-3282941470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110252","id":3282941470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DrbYe","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-11T23:21:00Z","updated_at":"2025-09-11T23:21:00Z","body":"Sure, I get that it is inconvenient but this is caused by the layout choice.\n\nThe linked proposal already tracks adding a convenience feature for it to \"fix\" bad polygon layouts at a performance cost.\nThere is no actionable bug or documentation fix here for the issue tracker.\n\nThe navigation system already provides better navmesh choices than the TileMap build-in navigation, e.g. NavigationRegion2D baked navmesh. Everything is better than the TileMap build-in tiny tiles layout that is only good for creating SISO situations.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3282941470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]